 - **One portable app bundle and one versioned domain contract.** The same Wasm package runs on every backend. The contract has a Go reference and a Rust mirror that pass one set of conformance vectors (`isolation/contract/`). *Live.*
-- **A target OS-independent isolation contract.** The intended contract includes a hardware domain per app, host-OS exclusion, measured identity, attestation, key and traffic binding, fail-closed verification and cleanup. The records document one VM per app on three host types, with processor-enforced host exclusion on SEV-SNP and pKVM-enforced exclusion on phones. Windows host exclusion remains unproven by us. The complete contract must not be inferred from per-app placement alone.
